Z||000001||Phaeton||06-05-2000||04:28 AM||||The scanner works and I can do it myself now.  Don't have any pictures less than two years old yet.<P>Fixed the Talon, turns out an inoperative oil cooler bypass temperature sensor caused all the symptoms.  The upside is how straightforward and simple the Fiero systems seem in comparison to the overengineered tight winding small displacement high tech rube goldberg contraptions found elsewhere.<P>Not that I would turn down a supercharger if offered.||||reg||12
Z||000002||fierospeeder||06-06-2000||05:23 AM||||thats a kewl car, <P>how did you figure out it was the sensor on the talon, i know diagnosing a car is a b*h <BR>My fiero, four cylinder, looks easy compared to my tbird, but then my beetle is like a four cylinder lawn mower engine.<P>I was wondering, do children take a lot of time out of your hands with your hobby, fieros.  My girlfriend has a child, not mine, but it does concern me in a way, she always tells me, its not my responsibility and i dont have to worry about it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lennyb4||06-06-2000||09:50 AM||||Hey speeder... I have 5 yes 5 kids ranging from ages of 12 to 9 months. I would have to say YES they do take alot of time and money from other things. BUT i would also have to say that having kids is one of the best experiances in life. Everyday when i go home i have 3 + 2 year old sons who come running outside yelling daddy, daddy we love you and end up wrapping themselves around me. And to be honest that is the best feeling in the world.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> : <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-06-2000||05:13 PM||||I have a 10 year old son.  I love my Fiero (those that know me understand), but if I had to chose...  Anyone want to buy a Fiero?  It would go that quickly.  Fortunately, my boy likes the Grape Ape almost as much as his old man. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  (Whew!)||||reg||1
